window.docContents[149].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Reductions.ReductionDsl.Samplers/#file-Computational___Specifications___Reductions___ReductionDsl___Samplers":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Reductions/ReductionDsl › Samplers.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 3 headline theorems depend on it 29 of 70 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nShared uniform samplers for ReductionDsl reductionsTrusted in part. The theorems of Computational/Theorems/ use every definition in this file except unifSamplers0, which is checked by Lean; the ones they use are part of what you must read to trust the result. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Coin-only uniform sampler templates attached to target interfaces via Iface.withSamp, providing uniform bits ($ᵗ Bool, cost 1), bounded indices in {0, …, N - 1} (cost bits N + 1), and uniform values on designated sampleable base sorts f : B → S.Base at declared block costs w (at least each sort's block size).\n\n\n\ndef sampleIndexL34–39 ↗#Uniform index in {0, …, N - 1}, returning 0 when N = 0.\n\ninductive UniformSamplerTagL41–45 ↗#Tags for coin-only uniform samplers: a bit, an index < N, or a sampleable base sort in B.\n\ndef unifSamplersL47–64 ↗#Shared uniform samplers over S for bits (cost 1), indices < N (cost bits N + 1), and base sorts f : B → S.Base at declared block costs w : B → ℕ.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 66–71): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesReductionDsl.unifSamplers0\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Reductions/ReductionDsl/Samplers.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Reductions.ReductionDsl.Samplers/#file-Computational___Specifications___Reductions___ReductionDsl___Samplers"},"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Object.Labels/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Object___Labels":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Object › Labels.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 221 of 269 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nDeclarations on this page (20)inductive SymKindinductive SymBindinductive SymSecstructure RawRelocstructure RawSecstructure RawSymstructure RawGroupstructure ExtractedObjstructure SliceOrigindef Discardeddef Resolvesdef SymNameDeriveddef UnclaimedSymNamedef CoversDataSlicedef ValidTextSlicedef ValidDataSlicedef RelocMatchesdef SliceRelocsMatchdef WeakOnlyUndefstructure LabelsFromObjects\n\nObject-Level Label ProvenanceDefines the pre-link relocatable object representation (ExtractedObj) emitted by trusted_extractor and the declarative provenance relation LabelsFromObjects, which ties a MultiPlacedLib's unrelocated sections, .bss zero-tails, permissions, alignments, exported entrypoints, STT_OBJECT symbols, external references, relocations, and STB_WEAK flags to extracted .o symbol and relocation tables independently of the final binary's .symtab.\n\n\n\ninductive SymKindL28–31 ↗#ELF symbol type (ELF64_ST_TYPE) in an extracted relocatable object.\n\ninductive SymBindL33–36 ↗#ELF symbol binding (ELF64_ST_BIND) in an extracted relocatable object.\n\ninductive SymSecL38–42 ↗#ELF symbol section index in an extracted relocatable object: undef (SHN_UNDEF), sec idx (allocated section idx of the object), or other (SHN_ABS, SHN_COMMON, or non-allocated).\n\nstructure RawRelocL44–51 ↗#Non-no-op ELF relocation record in a raw section (r_offset, mapped RelocKind or none when the relocation code is outside RelocKind, .symtab index, signed r_addend).\n\nstructure RawSecL53–65 ↗#Allocated (SHF_ALLOC, non-.eh_frame) section of an extracted .o file, carrying its unrelocated byte payload ([] when isNobits is true) and raw relocation records.\n\nstructure RawSymL67–77 ↗#One .symtab entry of an extracted .o file: rawName is the verbatim .strtab string and name is the extractor's demangled / disambiguated identifier.\n\nstructure RawGroupL79–85 ↗#SHT_GROUP section group with flag GRP_COMDAT of an extracted .o file: signature is the .strtab name of the group's sh_info symbol and members are the indices (into ExtractedObj.sections) of its extracted member sections.\n\nstructure ExtractedObjL87–94 ↗#Pre-link view of one relocatable .o file emitted directly by trusted_extractor, with its COMDAT groups in section header order.\n\nstructure SliceOriginL96–102 ↗#Half-open byte slice [start, start + len) of objs[oi].sections[si].\n\ndef DiscardedL104–111 ↗#lld drops section si of objs[oi]: it is a member of a COMDAT group whose signature an earlier group (in an earlier object, or earlier in the same object) already claimed.\n\ndef ResolvesL113–127 ↗#Static lld resolution of non-local name raw, with objs in link (parse) order: sy at (oi, k) is an STB_GLOBAL / STB_WEAK definition in allocated, non-Discarded section si, and every other non-local definition of raw is an STB_WEAK definition in an allocated section that sy beats (sy is STB_GLOBAL, or the first weak definition). Two STB_GLOBAL definitions, any SHN_ABS / SHN_COMMON / STB_GNU_UNIQUE competitor, and a Discarded winner fail closed.\n\ndef SymNameDerivedL129–131 ↗#sym is either base or base qualified with defining object objName (\"base [objName]\").\n\ndef UnclaimedSymNameL133–137 ↗#sym does not collide with any named .symtab entry (rawName or SymNameDerived) in objs, preventing synthetic labels on unnamed slices from spoofing real symbols.\n\ndef CoversDataSliceL139–142 ↗#sy is a named STT_OBJECT symbol covering [o.start, o.start + o.len) in o.si.\n\ndef ValidTextSliceL144–156 ↗#Block b is the exact unrelocated executable byte slice o of objs, with aligned bounds and symbols either backed by STT_FUNC entries in o or unclaimed synthetic labels.\n\ndef ValidDataSliceL158–170 ↗#Data entry d is the exact unrelocated non-executable slice o of objs (zero-filled of size o.len for SHT_NOBITS), with matching readOnly, alignment, and covering STT_OBJECT names, and with uncovered slices restricted to UnclaimedSymName.\n\ndef RelocMatchesL172–202 ↗#Placed RelocEntry r in a slice starting at sliceStart of object oi faithfully represents raw relocation rr: a STB_LOCAL symbol targets its own (non-Discarded) definition, and a non-local one (defined in objs[oi] or not) targets its Resolves winner across objs or, when nothing defines it, stays an external rawName. Fails closed on rr.kind = none, .other definitions, unresolvable names, or out-of-slice internal targets.\n\ndef SliceRelocsMatchL204–215 ↗#Relocations rs of slice o correspond 1-to-1 (via index bijection perm) to objs[o.oi].sections[o.si]'s relocations in [o.start, o.start + o.len).\n\ndef WeakOnlyUndefL217–222 ↗#x is referenced in objs only as undefined STB_WEAK and never defined as non-local (including SHN_ABS/SHN_COMMON) or in any allocated section.\n\nstructure LabelsFromObjectsL224–267 ↗#Declarative provenance tying lib to the pre-link objects objs via slice witnesses bO, dO:1. blocks_valid / data_valid: unrelocated bytes of non-Discarded sections, .bss zero-tails, permissions, alignments, and STT_FUNC / STT_OBJECT symbol names match objs;2. blocks_disjoint / data_disjoint / names_nodup: slices of the same (oi, si) are pairwise disjoint and block/data symbol names are injective and mutually disjoint;3. block_relocs / data_relocs: every raw relocation in every kept slice is accounted for 1-to-1 with exact target slice/offset (of the Resolves winner, for non-local symbols) or verbatim undefined .strtab rawName;4. exports_valid: each export e ∈ lib.exports is the Resolves winner of lib.elfSym e across objs, an STT_FUNC with sy.name = e;5. externs_valid: each block's externs are exactly its non-block call26/jump26 targets across lib.blocks (disjoint from block and data symbols), and weakRefs satisfy WeakOnlyUndef.objs lists the link inputs in lld parse order (an archive member at its extraction point). Out of scope by precondition: -shared / -pie symbol preemption, -r, --allow-multiple-definition, --wrap, --defsym, linker scripts, LTO, and .so inputs.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Object/Labels.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Object.Labels/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Object___Labels"}});